ui, time\n# click the address bar then search the Canada Gazette index for the first regulation\npyautogui.click(400, 90)  # address bar area\ntime.sleep(0.3)\npyautogui.typewrite('site:gazette.gc.ca \"Certain Wood Cabinet and Vanity Goods Surtax Order\" SOR 2026 registration date', interval=0.02)\ntime.sleep(0.2)\npyautogui.press('enter')","r":"I can see Chrome open with the address bar focused and a new tab ready. We previously opened Chrome to look up Canada Gazette pages to fill columns C and D in the spreadsheet; next I'll search the Canada Gazette site for the first regulation's page (to get the exact SOR number and registration date)."},{"n":4,"a":"import pyautogui, time\n# click the first search result title to open the Gazette page\npyautogui.click(360, 320)\ntime.sleep(1.5)","r":"The Chrome search results are visible and show the Gazette page for \"Certain Wood Cabinet and Vanity Goods Surtax Order\" (SOR/2026-169) and the index result. Next I'll open the Gazette result to read the exact registration date and SOR number."},{"n":5,"a":"import pyautogui, time\n# switch to LibreOffice Calc by clicking its dock icon (approx)\npyautogui.click(35, 405)\ntime.sleep(0.6)\n# click cell C3 and enter the SOR number\npyautogui.click(535+40, 461+10)  # center of C3 (approx)\ntime.sleep(0.2)\npyautogui.typewrite('SOR/2026-169', interval=0.02)\ntime.sleep(0.2)\n# click cell D3 and enter the registration date in YYYY-MM-DD\npyautogui.click(650+40, 461+1 …","r":"Reflection: I opened the Canada Gazette page for \"Certain Wood Cabinet and Vanity Goods Surtax Order\" and confirmed the registration line shows \"SOR/2026-169  July 31, 2026\". Next I'll return to the Calc window and enter SOR/2026-169 into C3 and 2026-07-31 into D3, then save the spreadsheet."},{"n":6,"a":"import pyautogui, time\n# save the LibreOffice Calc document\npyautogui.hotkey('ctrl', 's')\ntime.sleep(0.6)","r":"I can see the LibreOffice Calc window with the SOR number and registration date entered (C2 = 